# 3. RTM with Defect IDs

During testing, suppose we found **two defects**: one where the OTP is not received and another where the Signup button remains disabled even after entering valid details.

| Requirement ID | Requirement Description                                          | Test Case ID | Test Case Description                                                       | Defect ID  |
| -------------- | ---------------------------------------------------------------- | ------------ | --------------------------------------------------------------------------- | ---------- |
| **REQ-01**     | User can enter a valid mobile number/email.                      | **TC-01**    | Enter a valid mobile number/email and check that it is accepted.            | **—**      |
| **REQ-02**     | OTP should be sent for verification.                             | **TC-02**    | Enter a valid mobile number and check whether OTP is received.              | **DEF-01** |
| **REQ-03**     | Password should follow required rules.                           | **TC-03**    | Enter a valid password and verify that it is accepted.                      | **—**      |
| **REQ-04**     | Signup should work only when mandatory details are valid.        | **TC-04**    | Enter all valid mandatory details and check whether Signup becomes enabled. | **DEF-02** |
| **REQ-05**     | Successful registration should take the user to the home screen. | **TC-05**    | Complete signup with valid details and verify successful account creation.  | **—**      |

**Defects found:**

* **DEF-01:** OTP is not received after entering a valid mobile number.
* **DEF-02:** Signup button remains disabled even after all valid mandatory details are entered.

