# 4. Forward and Backward Traceability

**Forward traceability** means following a requirement forward to its related test case to make sure every requirement is actually tested. For example, **REQ-02 (OTP should be sent)** is linked forward to **TC-02**, which checks whether the OTP is received.

**Backward traceability** means starting from a test case and tracing it back to the requirement it was created to verify. For example, **TC-04** can be traced backward to **REQ-04**, because the test checks whether Signup works only when the required details are entered correctly. This helps make sure that no test case is unrelated to a requirement.

