# 5. Bi-Directional RTM – Login Feature

**Application:** Zomato-like Food Delivery App

| Requirement ID | Requirement                                                                 | Test Case ID | Test Case                                                           | Traceability   |
| -------------- | --------------------------------------------------------------------------- | ------------ | ------------------------------------------------------------------- | -------------- |
| **REQ-01**     | User should be able to log in using valid mobile number/email and password. | **TC-01**    | Login with valid credentials.                                       | REQ-01 ↔ TC-01 |
| **REQ-01**     | User should be able to log in using valid credentials.                      | **TC-02**    | Login with an incorrect password and verify that login is rejected. | REQ-01 ↔ TC-02 |
| **REQ-02**     | The system should not allow login when mandatory fields are blank.          | **TC-03**    | Leave mobile/email and password blank and click Login.              | REQ-02 ↔ TC-03 |
| **REQ-02**     | The system should validate mandatory login fields.                          | **TC-04**    | Enter a valid mobile number but leave the password blank.           | REQ-02 ↔ TC-04 |
| **REQ-03**     | After successful login, the user should be taken to the app home screen.    | **TC-05**    | Login with valid credentials and verify the home screen.            | REQ-03 ↔ TC-05 |

### Bi-directional view

**Forward:**
REQ-01 → TC-01, TC-02
REQ-02 → TC-03, TC-04
REQ-03 → TC-05

**Backward:**
TC-01 → REQ-01
TC-02 → REQ-01
TC-03 → REQ-02
TC-04 → REQ-02
TC-05 → REQ-03

This RTM makes it easy for the testing team to check that **every requirement has test coverage** and that **every test case has a valid requirement behind it**.

